- Docs/tests still reference `tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py` and `_command_tool_builders()`
- Actual file is missing (`ls tools/api_server` shows no `mcp_tools.py`)
- `tests/contract/test_surface_parity_matrix.py:16` imports it and fails collection
- `CLAUDE.md:376`, `.claude/skills/ww-scaffold-view/SKILL.md:58`, vendor integration ref `:24` are stale

3. “parity is strict only” stale wording
- `CLAUDE.md:388` says parity gate is run by `ww-build-test` in `strict` mode
- `ww-build-test` now runs parity in `standard+` (`.claude/skills/ww-build-test/SKILL.md:15`, `:59`)
- `ww-build-test` output block still says `PARITY (strict only)` (`.claude/skills/ww-build-test/SKILL.md:98`) which is internally inconsistent

4. Docs contradicting mandatory Parity Law / parity optionality
- `.claude/skills/ww-scaffold-view/SKILL.md:19` defaults to `ui+registry` (partial parity)
- `.claude/skills/ww-scaffold-view/SKILL.md:28-29` offers non-full parity scopes without a strong “spike only” warning
- `.claude/skills/ww-build-game/SKILL.md:331` marks Python parity as optional
- These conflict with `AGENTS.md:103-109` mandatory Parity Law

5. Wrong/deleted cross-references
- `CLAUDE.md:376` → `tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py` (missing file)
- `.claude/skills/ww-scaffold-view/SKILL.md:58` → `tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py` (missing file)
- `.pi/skills/wibwobdos/references/integrating-vendor-views.md:24` → `tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py` (missing file)
- `.pi/skills/wibwobdos/references/integrating-vendor-views.md:80-81` uses `/exec` endpoint (no route in `tools/api_server/main.py`; current endpoints include `/menu/command`, `/commands`, `/capabilities`)

**Fix Options (with tradeoffs)**

1. Align docs/tests to current architecture (FastAPI auto-MCP + minimal Node MCP)
- Fix docs to stop referencing `tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py`
- Rewrite parity tests to validate current surfaces (`/commands` and Node MCP minimal bridge assumptions)
- Tradeoff: fastest coherence fix, but weakens “all surfaces in one PR” enforcement until a richer MCP layer exists

2. Restore/implement Python MCP tool layer (`tools/api_server/mcp_tools.py`) and match docs/tests
- Reintroduce `mcp_tools.py` + `_command_tool_builders()`, expand Node MCP tools to parity expectations
- Tradeoff: strongest guardrail consistency, but materially larger engineering change

3. Hybrid (recommended short-term)
- Immediately patch docs/skills to remove false instructions and make parity policy accurate
- Mark broken parity tests as `xfail/skip` with explicit TODO issue, or update them to fail with a clearer message
- Add a temporary “current architecture” note in Parity Law sections
- Tradeoff: preserves momentum and reduces drift risk now, but still leaves incomplete enforcement until code/tests are finished

